## 1. Language & Communication Policy
- **Repository Content (Code, Commits, Docs):** English
- **Chat Output (Interaction with User):** German

## 2. Tech Stack

| Domain | Use |
|---|---|
| Runtime | Python {{ python_version }}, `uv` (package manager) |
| Build | `hatchling` (PEP 517) |
| Task Runner | `just` (see `justfile`) |
| Linting | `ruff` (lint + format) |
| Type Checking | `mypy` (strict mode) |
| Testing | `pytest` with markers (`unit`, `integration`, `system`) |
| Config | `python-dotenv` (`.env` files) |

## 3. Quality Gates

Run `just check` (alias: `just c`) **before every commit**. It runs:
1. `ruff check` — lint errors
2. `mypy` — type safety

Run `just fix` to auto-format and fix lint issues.

## 4. Testing Rules

1. Every test function **MUST** have exactly one marker: `@pytest.mark.unit`, `.integration`, or `.system`.
2. Tests live in `tests/unit/`, `tests/integration/`, `tests/system/` — matching their marker.
3. **Unit:** No I/O, no filesystem, no network. Fast (< 1s/test).
4. **Integration:** Real filesystem or external data. Self-contained.
5. **System:** Full pipeline end-to-end.

| Command | Scope |
|---|---|
| `just test` | Unit + Integration (daily driver) |
| `just test-all` | All three tiers |
| `just test-unit` | Unit only |
| `just test-int` | Integration only |
| `just test-system` | System only |

## 5. Commit Rules

Follow **[docs/development/commit.md](docs/development/commit.md)** strictly:
- Conventional Commits format: `<type>(<scope>): <subject>`
- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `chore`, `test`
- Subject: lowercase, imperative mood, ≤ 72 chars, no period
- Prefer small, focused commits over large monolithic ones

